{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"batch_id\": \"multi_batch_11\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_9863bdaea932f391\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_9863bdaea932f391/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Japanese honorific consistency review\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_898515634b0ff806f981c22e\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that the model changes honorific level when addressing the same person and asks whether others are seeing it.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether Japanese QA can examine the exact sentence endings. Verbatim quote: \\\"Can Japanese QA examine the exact sentence endings?\\\"\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ directs Korean or Japanese register-shift cases to the appropriate language QA with exact sentence endings and surrounding context, requires checking quotations and addressee changes, and says the grade depends on demonstrated impact rather than a shift alone warranting a major penalty.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current instructions require language QA to establish context and impact for disputed locale-specific cases; register grades distinguish materially disruptive confirmed inconsistency, localized inappropriate shifts, and justified variation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:db772378\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The tutor's report and the QA tutor's question contain no exact sentence endings, surrounding dialogue, or assessment resolving the reported honorific change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 25 Japanese review record describes M11-JA-022 changing from polite endings to plain form, with preceding dialogue missing and the addressee unestablished; it records a routed review awaiting complete dialogue, not a completed assessment, score, or approved general honorific rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multi-japanese-review-pending@1.0:124c6b92\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that the model changes honorific level while addressing the same person.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether Japanese QA can examine the exact sentence endings; the thread contains no assessment resolving the reported change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U003\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ directs register-shift cases to the appropriate language QA with exact sentence endings and surrounding context, and says a shift alone does not justify a major penalty.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier Japanese review record for M11-JA-022 remained awaiting complete dialogue and recorded no completed assessment or approved general honorific rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multi-japanese-review-pending@1.0:124c6b92\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Ask a language specialist to review. Instruction: Route the reported honorific-level change to Japanese language QA with exact sentence endings and surrounding context for a case-specific assessment. Draft to copy: Please review a reported Japanese honorific-level change: a tutor reports that the model changes level while addressing the same person. A QA tutor asks whether Japanese QA can examine the exact sentence endings.\\n\\nFor the reporting tutor: please provide the exact sentence endings and surrounding dialogue.\\n\\nFor Japanese language QA: please check quotations, addressee changes, and the effect in context. Under the current FAQ, any grade depends on demonstrated impact; do not assign a major penalty from the presence of a shift alone. Scope: This referral concerns the reported change; whether it is an error and how it should be graded depend on the case-specific context and impact.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\", \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\", \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:db772378\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The current FAQ assigns these cases to language QA, and the instructions make context and demonstrated impact necessary for grading. A specialist review fits the unresolved report without assuming that the change is an error.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\", \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\", \"k:multilingual-eval-instructions@1.2:db772378\", \"k:multi-japanese-review-pending@1.0:124c6b92\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): A tutor reports a same-addressee honorific change, and the QA tutor's question about Japanese QA review remains without a case assessment in the thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_898515634b0ff806f981c22e\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_898515634b0ff806f981c22e is UNRESOLVED: The tutor reports the change, and the QA tutor asks whether Japanese QA can examine the endings. The thread contains no answer or assessment resolving the report.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity LOW: One tutor reports a specific honorific inconsistency. The thread does not report conflicting scoring decisions, inability to work, or broader disruption; a case-specific review is proportionate.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:recurrence\", \"kind\": \"HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE\", \"text\": \"Retrieved records show this problem occurred before.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:multi-japanese-review-pending@1.0:124c6b92\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U003\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U003 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927633.000154\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_898515634b0ff806f981c22e\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927633.000154\", \"author_id\": \"U003\", \"author_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:53:53.000154Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U003\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"reactions\": [{\"name\": \"eyes\", \"users\": [\"U001\"]}], \"excerpt\": \"Anyone else seeing this? The model changes honorific level when addressing the same person.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_MULTI_GENERAL:1790927679.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_898515634b0ff806f981c22e\", \"thread_id\": \"1790927633.000154\", \"author_id\": \"U002\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-02T07:54:39.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U003\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Can Japanese QA examine the exact sentence endings?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}], \"retrieved_sources\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:c080929d\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multilingual-eval-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Multilingual Evaluation — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Register and honorifics\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multilingual-eval-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"approved\"}, \"excerpt\": \"## Register and honorifics\\n\\n### Q: Who scores Korean or Japanese register shifts?\\nRoute the case to appropriate Korean or Japanese language QA with exact sentence endings and surrounding context. Check quotations and addressee changes. The task-quality grade depends on demonstrated impact; do not assign a major penalty from the presence of a shift alone.\\n\\n### Q: Spanish tú versus usted inconsistency — major or minor?\\nAsk Spanish QA to check addressee, intended formality and discourse context. An unjustified shift can be an error, but its grade needs a case-specific rationale.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:multi-korean-scoped-result@1.0:5b489480\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multi-korean-scoped-result@1.0\", \"title\": \"Scoped Korean finding confirmed by the TL\", \"sections\": [\"Specialist finding\", \"TL confirmation\", \"Result and limits\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multi-korean-scoped-result\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"expert_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"OUT_OF_SCOPE\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-14T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-14T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"batch_id\": \"multi_batch_10\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"other_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"assessment_recorded\", \"outcome_status\": \"resolved_for_scoped_case\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (expert_review; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: assessment_recorded; outcome_status: resolved_for_scoped_case) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# Scoped Korean finding confirmed by the TL\\n\\n## Specialist finding\\nHana reviewed the complete paragraph for M10-KO-017. The casual sentence was a quoted utterance from a different speaker, and the surrounding narration retained its polite register. She found no unsupported shift by the narrator.\\n\\n## TL confirmation\\nAlex confirmed no register-consistency penalty for this exact quoted-speaker case. The finding does not authorize a casual switch while addressing the same person without a discourse reason.\\n\\n## Result and limits\\nThe batch-10 question for M10-KO-017 is resolved. Later same-addressee cases require their own context; an older favorable ruling cannot be transferred merely because both texts contain polite and casual endings.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:multi-japanese-backup-assignment-deferred@1.0:64536199\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multi-japanese-backup-assignment-deferred@1.0\", \"title\": \"Defer a proposed Japanese QA backup assignment\", \"sections\": [\"Evidence available at review\", \"Prior ThreadSense advice\", \"TL response\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multi-japanese-backup-assignment-deferred\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"advice_review\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NO_TL_APPROVAL\", \"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-28T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-28T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"batch_id\": \"multi_batch_11\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"NO_APPROVAL_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_deferred\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_deferred\", \"execution_status\": \"not_executed\", \"outcome_status\": \"open\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (advice_review; decision_status: tl_deferred; execution_status: not_executed; outcome_status: open) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# Defer a proposed Japanese QA backup assignment\\n\\n## Evidence available at review\\n\\nYuki (U019, Japanese QA) had not confirmed availability for the September 30 morning review slot. Leo (U007) had an open calendar slot, but the project roster records Spanish expertise for Leo, not Japanese. No alternate Japanese specialist or reviewed Japanese case was supplied with this request.\\n\\nThe staffing question remains open. No reassignment, specialist opinion, or resolution of a register question is recorded here.\\n\\n## Prior ThreadSense advice\\n\\nAssign Leo as the September 30 backup for the Japanese QA queue because his calendar shows an available slot.\\n\\n## TL response\\n\\nDefer this assignment. Availability does not establish Japanese expertise. Keep Yuki as the named Japanese reviewer and confirm her slot; if she is unavailable, bring me an appropriately qualified alternative. Do not route Japanese scoring decisions to Leo based only on this calendar opening.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:multi-japanese-review-pending@1.0:124c6b92\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"PRIOR_DECISION\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multi-japanese-review-pending@1.0\", \"title\": \"Japanese register review awaiting complete context\", \"sections\": [\"Case packet\", \"TL routing\", \"State\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multi-japanese-review-pending\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"decision\", \"record_kind\": \"expert_referral\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\", \"enactment\": {\"status\": \"NOT_ENACTED\", \"missing\": [\"NOT_A_POLICY_CHANGE\", \"NO_ENACTMENT_EVIDENCE\"]}}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-25T15:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"batch_id\": \"multi_batch_11\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"same_batch\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"actor\": \"U001\", \"actor_relation\": \"RECORD_AUTHORITY\", \"approval_status\": \"EXPLICIT_SOURCE_MARKER\", \"provenance\": \"synthetic_manual_record\"}, \"authorship\": {\"verified\": false, \"basis\": \"NO_AUTHOR_RECORDED\"}, \"recorded_states\": {\"status\": \"tl_approved\", \"decision_status\": \"tl_approved\", \"execution_status\": \"routed\", \"outcome_status\": \"awaiting_context\"}, \"excerpt\": \"[PRIOR RECORD (expert_referral; decision_status: tl_approved; execution_status: routed; outcome_status: awaiting_context) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# Japanese register review awaiting complete context\\n\\n## Case packet\\nM11-JA-022 was reported as starting in です/ます and ending in plain form. The supplied excerpt omitted the preceding dialogue and did not establish whether the closing sentence addressed the same person.\\n\\n## TL